+# INP diagnostics
+
+The static page loads the self-hosted `web-vitals` 6.2.3 attribution build.
+It measures real INP candidates, including the metric's outlier handling and
+page lifecycle behavior, rather than treating every long event as INP.
+
+Set the `inp-report-endpoint` meta tag in `index.html` to an analytics ingestion
+URL to collect reports. No collector is included in this static app. The endpoint
+must accept POST bodies containing JSON with a `text/plain` content type;
+cross-origin collectors must allow the site's origin for the fetch fallback.
+Reports use `sendBeacon`, falling back to `fetch` with `keepalive` if needed.
+An empty endpoint disables network reporting. Each report also dispatches the
+`inp-diagnostic` window event with the JSON-safe report in `event.detail`.
+
+Reports include the metric ID, value in milliseconds, rating, interaction label,
+input delay, processing duration, and presentation delay. Where available, they
+also include script/rendering totals and the longest overlapping script's URL,
+function, character position, forced layout time, and affected delay phase.
+Use the largest delay phase to narrow an investigation: input delay suggests
+existing main-thread work, processing duration suggests interaction handlers,
+and presentation delay suggests work before the next frame. These are clues,
+not proof of a particular root cause.
+
+Candidate updates are enabled. Upsert by metric `id` (using the latest received
+value), rather than counting updates as separate visits. The library also
+reports on visibility changes and handles back/forward cache restoration.
+Unsupported Event Timing browsers produce no INP report. Without Long Animation
+Frames, the delay breakdown remains available but script details may be absent.
+
+Interaction labels come from explicitly authored `data-inp-target` attributes,
+falling back to the element tag; no text, input values, or arbitrary DOM IDs are
+collected. Page/script URLs omit queries and fragments. Keep labels and URL
+paths free of sensitive data, and apply your analytics collection policy when
+configuring a collector.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for Node-based attribution and transport checks. No browser is
+required. After upgrading `web-vitals`, run `pnpm vendor:web-vitals` and commit
+the lockfile, vendor module, and license so the site still needs no build step.
